                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On Thursday, April 22, 1954, at 4 p.m., Secretary of State John Foster Dulles, British Foreign Secretary
                        Anthony Eden, and French Foreign
                    Minister Georges Bidault met at the Quai
                    d’Orsay to discuss the Geneva Conference, which convened on April 26. For the
                    record of this tripartite meeting, see <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg_544"
                        >volume XVI, page 544</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
